WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.008
[opening theme music playing]

01:03.605 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:06.066 --> 01:07.609
[TV playing indistinctly]

01:07.692 --> 01:10.028
[reporter] Are they spies?
They're not, are they?

01:10.528 --> 01:13.031
Because I heard one of them
is from Busan, right?

01:13.114 --> 01:14.574
[officer 2] Look, Mr. Kim,

01:14.657 --> 01:17.118
these kids don't get to decide
what they are.

01:17.202 --> 01:18.703
Namsan decides.

01:21.956 --> 01:23.541
You ate everything.

01:23.625 --> 01:24.709
Were you hungry?

01:27.045 --> 01:30.090
[officer 1] Look down, you.
You think this is funny?

01:30.673 --> 01:33.343
We keep feeding them.
That's why kids keep running away.

01:33.426 --> 01:36.638
These hooligans will have to return
to Namsan and come back to their senses.

01:36.721 --> 01:38.973
Couple of life sentences.
That would be patriotic.

01:43.686 --> 01:45.021
Look at that.

01:45.105 --> 01:45.980
They're in love.

01:46.648 --> 01:48.274
[officer 1 chuckles]

01:49.943 --> 01:51.736
Are you out of your mind, punk?

01:52.612 --> 01:54.989
[scoffs] You're in the big city now,
Jeju boy.

01:55.073 --> 01:56.491
Roll your sleeve down again.

01:56.574 --> 02:00.328
So you think you can block a hit
from a big-city police officer, do ya?

02:00.411 --> 02:02.622
-You little brat!
-Are you even in charge here?

02:04.582 --> 02:06.209
[breathing nervously]

02:06.918 --> 02:10.672
Are you who decides what happens to us?
Or do you answer to someone else?

02:10.755 --> 02:13.299
Oh, how sweet. Double trouble.

02:13.383 --> 02:14.801
[officer 1] Why you little…

02:14.884 --> 02:16.970
You hear this chick talk back to me?
How dare you?

02:17.053 --> 02:19.180
Is that against the law?
Am I going to jail now?

02:19.264 --> 02:20.974
Will I be serving a life sentence?

02:21.474 --> 02:23.059
You're one of those girls, right?

02:23.560 --> 02:25.937
A girl who smokes and wears miniskirts!

02:26.020 --> 02:27.564
Am I going to Namsan for wearing skirts?

02:28.523 --> 02:30.608
That lady reported us as runaways, right?

02:30.692 --> 02:33.069
There's certainly nothing more
she could have accused us of.

02:33.153 --> 02:34.195
[officer 1] More than what?

02:34.279 --> 02:36.364
Did you steal something too?
What did you steal?

02:36.447 --> 02:39.659
This boy and I are not sitting here in
this police station because we're thieves.

02:39.742 --> 02:41.578
We're… We are just sitting here

02:41.661 --> 02:43.121
because we are just minors,

02:43.204 --> 02:45.456
and we're in need of
Busan police protection.

02:46.499 --> 02:49.419
All we need is to sit quietly
and wait for our guardians to pick us up.

02:49.502 --> 02:52.046
-You expect special treatment?
-I expect you not to hit him.

02:52.755 --> 02:54.632
[officer 2 scoffs, laughs]

02:57.051 --> 02:59.512
This girl… is a politician.

02:59.596 --> 03:04.100
Oh my.
The Romeo and Juliet of Jeju Island.

03:04.184 --> 03:06.394
So why aren't you calling
your mothers, then, huh?

03:06.477 --> 03:07.604
There's no need for that.

03:07.687 --> 03:10.190
The boy's mom has been
camping out front all day long.

03:11.065 --> 03:12.192
[officer 1] What?

03:12.775 --> 03:13.651
Tall and handsome.

03:15.069 --> 03:16.237
And the naughty look.

03:17.989 --> 03:18.907
There she is now.

03:20.992 --> 03:21.826
Ma?

03:21.910 --> 03:23.328
[breathing anxiously]

03:25.622 --> 03:26.456
Mom.

03:28.249 --> 03:29.334
[Gye-ok sighs]

03:31.002 --> 03:31.836
The suitcase?

03:32.629 --> 03:34.589
-Where is it?
-Huh?

03:35.381 --> 03:37.634
-Where is my gold, huh? Huh?
-[Gwan-sik] Huh?

03:38.134 --> 03:39.135
Damn it.

03:39.928 --> 03:42.722
My gold. Good Lord. [sighs]

03:42.805 --> 03:45.975
Where's my gold frog, huh?
Where's my golden frog?

03:46.768 --> 03:48.186
[car horn honking]

03:51.648 --> 03:53.650
[intriguing music playing]

03:59.155 --> 04:01.574
Well? It's real gold, isn't it?

04:03.451 --> 04:04.285
It is.

04:04.369 --> 04:05.787
[laughing]

04:06.496 --> 04:08.331
That husband of mine.

04:08.831 --> 04:11.209
I swear, he does this
for every anniversary.

04:11.292 --> 04:13.544
He just can't wait
to buy me something nice.

04:13.628 --> 04:14.545
[both chuckle]

04:14.629 --> 04:15.880
[store owner] Is that right?

04:17.173 --> 04:18.800
Look, it's just,

04:18.883 --> 04:21.052
our cabinet is practically
filled with jewelry.

04:21.886 --> 04:23.972
I wanna get rid of what's out of fashion.

04:24.555 --> 04:26.057
But they're still worth a lot.

04:26.140 --> 04:26.975
Are they?

04:27.684 --> 04:30.103
You gave me a good price the last time.

04:30.770 --> 04:33.356
That was summer, and you said
it was your anniversary then.

04:34.023 --> 04:37.402
So? Is your anniversary
in the summer or not?

04:37.485 --> 04:40.196
At the time, you said
your husband got you a gold bracelet.

04:42.740 --> 04:43.908
No, it's…

04:44.701 --> 04:45.660
it's in the spring.

04:47.036 --> 04:48.371
Mm, I see.

04:49.956 --> 04:50.873
Besides,

04:52.208 --> 04:53.126
does it matter?

04:54.752 --> 04:56.212
[woman] I hope you enjoyed your stay.

04:56.713 --> 04:58.798
-[man] How much do I owe you?
-[woman] 300 won.

04:58.881 --> 04:59.966
[Gye-ok] Give it to me.

05:00.049 --> 05:02.302
-[woman] No, give it to me.
-[Gye-ok] Give it to me.

05:03.261 --> 05:04.220
[woman] Give it to me.

05:04.971 --> 05:08.141
-Don't mind her. I'll take that.
-Ah! Don't you dare give it to her.

05:08.224 --> 05:09.225
-That money is mine.
-Hey!

05:09.309 --> 05:12.478
I'm the owner here!
What would he pay you for? It's my motel.

05:13.104 --> 05:16.232
It's her motel and my money.
I had a suitcase, and this woman stole it.

05:16.316 --> 05:18.276
So I'm collecting the money
until her debt is paid.

05:18.359 --> 05:19.402
She's lying. Give it here.

05:19.485 --> 05:20.903
You know what? I'll come back later.

05:20.987 --> 05:22.655
Wait, wait, wait, wait! Hold on.

05:22.739 --> 05:24.449
Where are you going? Wait!

05:25.533 --> 05:27.368
[screams] Damn it.

05:28.661 --> 05:29.495
[sighs]

05:29.579 --> 05:31.414
-What's your plan now?
-[groans]

05:31.497 --> 05:32.874
You gonna spend the night?

05:34.250 --> 05:37.086
You know why
we don't have thieves on Jeju Island?

05:37.170 --> 05:39.088
Because Jeju hospitality is top-notch?

05:39.172 --> 05:40.423
We wear them down.

05:40.506 --> 05:42.508
We don't give in until they're broken.

05:42.592 --> 05:46.429
We keep the pressure on until the victim
has driven the robber completely insane.

05:46.512 --> 05:47.388
That's why we don't.

05:47.472 --> 05:48.639
[hisses]

05:49.682 --> 05:52.060
Wow. Damn Jeju witch.

05:52.143 --> 05:53.853
[frustrated grunt]

05:53.936 --> 05:55.229
[woman] You're the crazy one.

05:55.313 --> 05:57.774
Do you hear me? You're the crazy one.

05:57.857 --> 06:00.943
Just leave me alone! Damn you!

06:01.027 --> 06:03.946
I'm taking back what I'm owed,
and that's all there is.

06:04.447 --> 06:06.074
So I'll be here all day and night

06:06.157 --> 06:08.951
until I've recovered
the full cost of my golden toad.

06:09.035 --> 06:09.911
What?

06:09.994 --> 06:11.537
Did you say your "toad"?

06:12.163 --> 06:13.581
The cost of my golden toad, yeah.

06:13.664 --> 06:15.458
Really? Ah!

06:15.541 --> 06:18.961
So the gold frog is a gold toad now?
Not when I saw it!

06:20.588 --> 06:22.048
You really stepped in it now.

06:22.131 --> 06:24.884
She's got you there, Mom.
Better give her the frog back.

06:25.635 --> 06:26.469
[sighs]

06:26.552 --> 06:29.305
I'll take your word for it.
Toads are bigger anyway.

06:30.515 --> 06:33.017
Oh, I see. You think you can rob me, eh?

06:33.101 --> 06:35.395
I'll bet you have a criminal history,
don't you?

06:35.478 --> 06:37.021
-[scoffs]
-Maybe we should call the cops.

06:37.105 --> 06:38.481
-Just wait, you--
-What the--

06:38.564 --> 06:40.233
-You want me to call the cops?
-Hey, ladies!

06:40.316 --> 06:41.275
-Do you?
-Call them!

06:41.359 --> 06:43.111
-Knock it off!
-What the hell do you want?

06:43.194 --> 06:44.529
[quirky music playing]

06:44.612 --> 06:45.780
[both panting]

06:45.863 --> 06:49.325
Did you think we wouldn't check
the jewelry store? Sheesh.

06:51.160 --> 06:52.286
[sighs]

06:53.246 --> 06:56.457
You do realize this makes ten offenses?

06:56.541 --> 06:58.709
Come on, think of your child for once.

06:58.793 --> 06:59.752
Let's go.

06:59.836 --> 07:02.130
Don't take anyone from Jeju
while I'm gone.

07:03.172 --> 07:04.173
[officer 2] Take her away.

07:04.257 --> 07:05.800
-Get your hands off me.
-Take her away.

07:05.883 --> 07:07.760
[Gye-ok] Good Lord.
She's committed ten offenses?

07:07.844 --> 07:09.303
[woman] Oh, get your hands off me!

07:09.971 --> 07:11.681
Ain't she a handful?

07:11.764 --> 07:13.141
Ay, ay, ay.

07:14.725 --> 07:15.893
[music fades]

07:18.855 --> 07:20.022
[woman grunts]

07:24.235 --> 07:26.487
Hey, you brats!
You're gonna pay for that fan.

07:26.571 --> 07:28.114
You hear me? You're gonna pay.

07:28.197 --> 07:29.907
Did you have a circus in there or what?

07:30.408 --> 07:32.076
How'd you even break it
in the first place?

07:32.160 --> 07:33.786
You're a couple of filthy animals!

07:33.870 --> 07:35.788
-Hey, stop pushing me!
-[siren wailing]

07:38.666 --> 07:40.668
[upbeat music playing]

07:43.713 --> 07:44.714
[chuckles]

07:44.797 --> 07:45.882
Ta-da!

07:48.551 --> 07:50.595
[music fades]

07:51.179 --> 07:52.513
[sighs]

07:53.890 --> 07:55.183
[Gye-ok] Bought the tofu already?

07:56.601 --> 07:57.643
[Gwan-sik] Uh, no.

07:58.186 --> 07:59.604
I didn't buy the tofu.

07:59.687 --> 08:01.105
A girl bought it for us.

08:06.402 --> 08:07.320
Your, uh,

08:08.237 --> 08:11.699
birthday rings weren't in the bag.
Did you not take them when you left?

08:11.782 --> 08:13.701
Everything we took was in the bag.

08:15.828 --> 08:18.247
[groans] I can't believe this.

08:19.373 --> 08:20.708
You're just like your dad.

08:21.292 --> 08:23.461
Both of you, just like dogs.

08:28.090 --> 08:29.509
Ae-sun, let's take you home.

08:29.592 --> 08:31.594
[upbeat music resumes]

08:33.387 --> 08:36.015
My girl, you've really done it this time.

08:36.098 --> 08:37.975
YESTERDAY WAS YOUR SPRING

08:38.059 --> 08:40.520
You will never hear the end of this one.

08:41.103 --> 08:42.313
FACULTY OFFICE

08:48.528 --> 08:50.321
[teacher 1] She should've just left
on her own.

08:50.404 --> 08:52.823
Did she have to drag down
the boy with her?

08:54.867 --> 08:56.661
-[bell dings]
-[whistle blows]

08:58.120 --> 09:00.957
[teacher 2] That boy is one of
the top four runners in all of Jeju.

09:01.040 --> 09:03.793
[teacher 3] Well, she's
the poet of class eight?

09:03.876 --> 09:05.253
[teacher 1] Poet, my foot.

09:05.336 --> 09:08.047
Did she run away
with her boyfriend for poetry?

09:08.798 --> 09:09.966
[sobs]

09:21.519 --> 09:22.562
[sighs]

09:25.231 --> 09:28.651
POEMS OF YU CHI-HWAN
HANDKERCHIEF OF ETERNAL NOSTALGIA

09:34.448 --> 09:36.200
EXPULSION NOTICE
OH AE-SUN

09:36.284 --> 09:40.371
DUE TO AN UNAUTHORIZED RUNAWAY
AND DISRUPTIVE BEHAVIOR

09:42.206 --> 09:44.709
[man] You've completely
ruined your life with this.

09:45.459 --> 09:48.337
Everyone on this island knows
everything about everybody.

09:48.421 --> 09:50.673
I can't even show my face at the factory.

09:51.173 --> 09:53.968
Now you've gone and dragged
this family's name through the mud.

09:54.051 --> 09:55.886
Like your son painted it gold.

09:56.804 --> 09:58.472
You can't compare him with her.

09:58.556 --> 10:00.516
No, when a man is
financially unsuccessful,

10:00.600 --> 10:03.144
he may lose a house, but that's different.

10:03.227 --> 10:04.979
Why do you insist on bringing him up?

10:05.062 --> 10:08.024
Did he run a business,
or did he gamble it away?

10:08.524 --> 10:09.942
And now what? Huh?

10:10.026 --> 10:11.360
What are you gonna do now?

10:11.861 --> 10:13.863
You won't work at a factory.
You can't get married.

10:13.946 --> 10:15.740
Will you live here as a spinster?

10:17.199 --> 10:18.409
[sighs]

10:21.579 --> 10:22.747
What about him?

10:22.830 --> 10:24.498
What did that awful boy say?

10:25.791 --> 10:26.917
[melodic piano music playing]

10:27.001 --> 10:28.836
[grunts, pants]

10:28.919 --> 10:29.795
Look there.

10:29.879 --> 10:32.298
See the grandmother who raised you
since you were a baby?

10:32.381 --> 10:34.884
Look what you've done to her!
Is it just you that matters?

10:34.967 --> 10:36.510
What would the ancestors think?

10:36.594 --> 10:37.845
I'm the one marrying her.

10:38.638 --> 10:39.639
Not the ancestors.

10:43.809 --> 10:45.561
[man] What would they think about it?

10:45.645 --> 10:48.981
That Gwan-sik brought home an orphan wife
with only a middle-school degree?

10:49.732 --> 10:53.235
Who brings a daughter-in-law like that
into a high-class family?

10:53.986 --> 10:55.404
Only a middle-school degree?

10:55.488 --> 10:58.074
That's right. You think
they'd give her a high school diploma

10:58.157 --> 10:59.742
after that stunt you pulled?

11:01.202 --> 11:03.204
Go on! Live there if you want.

11:03.704 --> 11:06.165
Let your dreams die.
Live there as his fiancée.

11:06.248 --> 11:08.542
There are all kinds of rumors
spreading about you two.

11:08.626 --> 11:10.544
Good luck now marrying anybody else!

11:10.628 --> 11:12.213
[Yi-suk] She can't go over there.

11:12.296 --> 11:14.840
Their grandmother…
She was so upset, she fainted.

11:15.383 --> 11:17.802
Congratulations,
that's the best thing yet.

11:17.885 --> 11:19.595
You nearly killed a grandmother too.

11:19.679 --> 11:22.765
On top of sneaking out at night
and completely wrecking your life.

11:23.683 --> 11:24.558
[scoffs]

11:25.184 --> 11:26.435
It was only a suspension.

11:26.519 --> 11:28.437
Oh yeah? That's good for you.

11:28.521 --> 11:29.855
But why is she… Why did they…

11:31.649 --> 11:33.401
Why is she expelled from school?

11:33.484 --> 11:36.654
You can't even do soldering
without a high school diploma, damn it.

11:36.737 --> 11:39.532
-But why is she the only one?
-[woman] Is it possible you don't know?

11:39.615 --> 11:42.952
You both ran away,
but it's brave when a boy does it.

11:43.035 --> 11:45.204
When a girl acts out of love,
it's frivolous.

11:45.287 --> 11:48.332
Did you ruin her life
because you didn't know any better?

11:49.458 --> 11:50.876
It was my idea.

11:51.585 --> 11:53.170
This idiot just followed along.

11:53.879 --> 11:54.922
You deserve him.

11:56.674 --> 11:58.926
[man] Take him off the family registry.
Take him off.

11:59.927 --> 12:01.512
No one's punishing my baby.

12:01.595 --> 12:03.264
Ae-sun should get punished.

12:03.848 --> 12:06.308
You don't tear down the house
because you find a maggot.

12:06.392 --> 12:09.353
What can we do about someone else's kid?
It's our boy who's head over heels.

12:09.437 --> 12:11.522
[spits] Mark my words.

12:11.605 --> 12:14.650
When I get my hands on her,
I'll beat that girl real good.

12:14.734 --> 12:17.403
No, you won't. What would that accomplish?

12:17.486 --> 12:20.114
You never got anywhere with me
by pulling my hair.

12:20.197 --> 12:22.658
So what? I lost you.
I won't lose my grandson.

12:24.493 --> 12:26.829
If you wanna coax a chicken
out of its coop,

12:26.912 --> 12:29.457
you don't go in and beat it with a stick.

12:29.540 --> 12:33.919
You have to lure it out with some worms.
If you chase after it, it's gone for good.

12:35.755 --> 12:38.716
They really locked you up with a spoon.
Good Lord.

12:39.216 --> 12:40.217
[tuts]

12:40.885 --> 12:41.844
Oh well.

12:43.053 --> 12:45.389
Oh. Oh my.

12:46.015 --> 12:48.642
Do they at least give you things to eat?

12:48.726 --> 12:49.643
Yes.

12:50.311 --> 12:53.397
They do. I'm not skipping any meals.

12:54.064 --> 12:55.274
[Gye-ok scoffs]

12:55.983 --> 12:57.151
Oh. [chuckles]

12:57.234 --> 12:58.819
Well, that's good to hear.

12:58.903 --> 13:01.405
My Gwan-sik, he hasn't eaten a thing.

13:01.906 --> 13:04.033
Why? Is he on a hunger strike?

13:04.116 --> 13:05.910
Oh, he would never.

13:05.993 --> 13:09.038
His father told me
not to feed him a grain of rice.

13:12.541 --> 13:15.669
Ae-sun, you know
I'd love to do something about this.

13:16.587 --> 13:17.963
But you know his grandma.

13:18.047 --> 13:20.674
She's always laying down the law.

13:21.300 --> 13:24.261
I married into the headstrong Yang family,

13:24.345 --> 13:26.639
and to this day,
I'm still paying the price.

13:27.139 --> 13:29.266
You know how stubborn the Yangs can be.

13:29.350 --> 13:33.479
Remember how Gwan-sik gave your family
a fish every day for ten years?

13:33.562 --> 13:34.605
Goodness.

13:35.397 --> 13:37.900
I gave your family cabbages sometimes.

13:40.528 --> 13:43.030
Where do you think Gwan-sik
gets that stubbornness?

13:43.113 --> 13:46.367
From his father, of course,
and now his father

13:46.450 --> 13:49.662
is trying to get him
entirely cut out of the family.

13:50.579 --> 13:51.705
Goodness.

13:52.289 --> 13:54.792
You know, he's really quite
a tiny man on the inside.

13:56.252 --> 13:59.213
But once I was so crazy about him,
we ran away together.

13:59.296 --> 14:00.130
[sighs]

14:00.214 --> 14:02.800
See, things don't stay
so lovey-dovey for long.

14:03.509 --> 14:05.010
Right until the wedding day,

14:05.094 --> 14:08.264
I believed him when he said
I was the only one for him.

14:08.347 --> 14:10.349
But as soon as we were married,

14:10.432 --> 14:13.269
he became a mama's boy
like you wouldn't believe.

14:13.352 --> 14:15.396
So think about it.

14:17.565 --> 14:20.609
You would feel so lonely in our household.

14:23.737 --> 14:24.738
Mrs. Yang?

14:25.322 --> 14:26.574
Yes, my dear?

14:28.951 --> 14:31.704
I wanted to ask you something,

14:31.787 --> 14:32.746
if I could?

14:35.291 --> 14:37.293
[sentimental music playing]

14:47.386 --> 14:48.470
[sighs]

14:51.307 --> 14:54.602
We can't afford to marry her off.
No one's happy about it.

14:55.895 --> 14:58.147
But we can't. Not one silver spoon.

14:58.230 --> 15:00.024
I'd still love her, with or without.

15:01.275 --> 15:03.611
Your family? Do they approve of her?

15:04.612 --> 15:05.946
Your grandmother's a shaman.

15:06.530 --> 15:08.407
You've heard what she says about the girl.

15:08.490 --> 15:10.951
She says she carries
her mother's ghost around with her.

15:11.952 --> 15:15.164
On this island, we don't believe
in God or Buddha but the Dragon King.

15:15.247 --> 15:17.750
Ignore his shamans at your own risk.

15:17.833 --> 15:18.667
[sighs]

15:19.209 --> 15:22.171
Ae-sun will live with me.
She won't live with my grandmother.

15:22.254 --> 15:24.006
I can guarantee she'll never hurt her.

15:24.089 --> 15:27.801
How you gonna do that? You moving out?
You got a house I don't know about?

15:30.137 --> 15:32.473
What are you doing?
Who said you had to take care of me?

15:32.556 --> 15:34.600
I'm not a rotten fish to get cheap.

15:35.351 --> 15:37.895
You keep her in there
with the fermenting jars?

15:37.978 --> 15:41.440
Just forget it already.
The least I can do is to save my pride.

15:41.523 --> 15:42.691
I want to marry you.

15:42.775 --> 15:46.236
Why? Because you think
it'll never happen for me if you don't?

15:46.320 --> 15:48.322
I'm going to marry a man
who's richer than you and…

15:48.405 --> 15:50.699
and a lot hotter,
and he'll have a nicer family than you.

15:50.783 --> 15:52.576
He's mad enough to take you.

15:52.660 --> 15:54.578
-Don't turn him down.
-Just watch me.

15:54.662 --> 15:55.996
I'll never marry him.

15:56.080 --> 15:58.248
I'll turn him down a million times.
You just watch!

16:03.462 --> 16:04.964
[lively upbeat music playing]

16:05.047 --> 16:06.215
[groans]

16:09.510 --> 16:11.637
[man] Hey, waitress. Bring us some tea.

16:12.221 --> 16:14.223
Ko-hyang, give them some tea.

16:14.306 --> 16:15.516
Yes, ma'am.

16:15.599 --> 16:17.017
Oh, welcome back, sir.

16:17.101 --> 16:20.354
So you raised two siblings
practically all by yourself?

16:22.147 --> 16:25.567
Based on that experience alone,
I already approve of you.

16:26.568 --> 16:27.403
Okay.

16:35.327 --> 16:38.038
[slurping loudly]

16:43.210 --> 16:46.130
So I heard you were
after a man from Seoul.

16:48.716 --> 16:49.967
You know… [sniffles]

16:50.718 --> 16:52.469
…I'm practically from Seoul myself.

16:53.303 --> 16:54.471
After Korea's independence,

16:54.555 --> 16:57.474
I got an education on the mainland
as good as any in Seoul.

16:58.642 --> 17:01.061
Had I not moved here after I got married,

17:01.729 --> 17:03.689
I could've been another Kim Du-han.

17:07.776 --> 17:08.736
My first marriage

17:09.236 --> 17:10.070
at the start.

17:11.947 --> 17:13.115
Are we getting that tea today?

17:23.375 --> 17:25.419
Don't worry too much about what I think.

17:26.003 --> 17:28.756
I mean, who says that it's wrong to love?

17:28.839 --> 17:30.340
[crunching]

17:30.424 --> 17:34.595
And, sure, I heard a few things
about your past through the grapevine,

17:35.095 --> 17:35.929
but still,

17:37.514 --> 17:39.475
I'm quite determined to seal the deal.

17:39.558 --> 17:41.060
[wistful music playing]

17:41.143 --> 17:43.645
I've crossed the Pacific many times,
so your little jaunt

17:43.729 --> 17:45.439
isn't such a big deal to me.

17:45.522 --> 17:49.026
As a man practically from Seoul,
I don't care what you did in the past.

17:50.194 --> 17:52.154
I heard second marriages work out better.

17:52.654 --> 17:54.740
The parties have an understanding.

17:54.823 --> 17:58.243
Honestly, the idea of getting married
to another virgin would be just

17:59.578 --> 18:00.996
such an inconvenience.

18:07.795 --> 18:10.297
You're not going to drink it?
It cost 50 won, Ae-sun.

18:14.301 --> 18:15.344
[rain pattering]

18:15.427 --> 18:19.014
Sure, he's been married before,
but he owns boats.

18:19.515 --> 18:21.558
And not just one boat either.

18:21.642 --> 18:24.937
Why, you can't look in the harbor
without seeing one of them.

18:26.438 --> 18:28.482
And on… and on top of everything,

18:28.982 --> 18:32.194
he'll pay for you to go to school.
Within ten years, at least.

18:33.028 --> 18:35.322
And if you really please them,

18:35.405 --> 18:38.992
they might even give you funds
to publish your own book of poetry.

18:41.161 --> 18:42.538
It's only two kids.

18:44.873 --> 18:46.250
At least it's not three.

18:47.543 --> 18:48.627
[Ae-sun sighs]

18:50.254 --> 18:52.923
I guess I'm born
to merely be a housekeeper.

18:54.424 --> 18:55.467
Oh gosh.

18:57.594 --> 18:59.763
The spring rain sure is lasting a while.

19:03.517 --> 19:05.561
It must be the tears of my mother.

19:09.231 --> 19:12.234
Maybe she's crying because this is
how I'm gonna get married.

19:24.037 --> 19:25.706
[music fades]

19:25.789 --> 19:28.417
Gwang-rye is spinning in her grave!

19:28.500 --> 19:29.501
[grunts]

19:30.085 --> 19:34.882
You've completely ruined the girl's life,
but apparently, you still like your rice!

19:34.965 --> 19:37.718
If you're so upset for her,
then you can marry your son to Ae-sun.

19:37.801 --> 19:38.677
How about that?

19:38.760 --> 19:40.971
But why are you making her a second wife?

19:41.555 --> 19:44.766
It's obvious that both of your families
are desperate to get rid of her.

19:44.850 --> 19:45.684
[frustrated sigh]

19:45.767 --> 19:48.312
Mak-cheon, you may be a shaman,

19:48.395 --> 19:50.814
but you have no right
to punish another family's girl.

19:50.898 --> 19:53.275
If you force Ae-sun to marry that man,

19:53.358 --> 19:55.444
I'll never believe another word you say.

19:56.111 --> 19:58.280
We need goodness of the heart, I tell you.

19:58.363 --> 19:59.781
Goodness of the heart!

19:59.865 --> 20:01.617
Will you shut up?!

20:02.201 --> 20:03.452
Ae-sun's getting married?

20:03.535 --> 20:04.828
[disgusted groan]

20:07.706 --> 20:09.666
MADAM BAEK GI-NAM'S 60TH BIRTHDAY

20:14.630 --> 20:16.798
Is that really
what you're giving my family?

20:16.882 --> 20:18.634
A used gift set?

20:18.717 --> 20:20.385
[man] This is American-made.

20:22.638 --> 20:24.348
Well, made in Korea, but close enough.

20:24.932 --> 20:27.434
Besides, it's all the same
once they eat it, right?

20:28.018 --> 20:30.771
I can't stand
all these meaningless formalities.

20:31.480 --> 20:35.943
The whole wedding business is just
one useless formal gesture after another.

20:36.026 --> 20:38.904
Just a way of robbing people
of their money. Huh?

20:42.491 --> 20:45.035
Honestly, the white dress
doesn't really matter to me.

20:45.118 --> 20:46.453
That's for first weddings.

20:47.371 --> 20:49.623
We can just look nice
and take a few pictures.

20:49.706 --> 20:53.335
Seeing as, technically,
it's not the first time for either of us.

20:53.418 --> 20:54.336
[clears throat]

20:54.419 --> 20:56.171
So, speaking of,

20:57.130 --> 20:59.633
I was actually curious about something.

21:00.550 --> 21:03.011
So, uh…

21:03.095 --> 21:04.471
Mm.

21:04.554 --> 21:05.764
About Busan.

21:10.477 --> 21:12.145
Does your mother know about this?

21:14.064 --> 21:15.232
[Yi-suk] Oh my.

21:15.315 --> 21:17.693
You must've cleared out your entire store.

21:17.776 --> 21:20.654
-Good Lord.
-[Yi-suk] This isn't a gift. It's robbery.

21:20.737 --> 21:23.031
[Gwan-sik] I'll make sure
Ae-sun never goes hungry.

21:23.532 --> 21:25.742
I can give her a mackerel
at least once a day.

21:25.826 --> 21:29.121
It isn't wartime anymore.
No one's worried about starving.

21:31.123 --> 21:32.499
Aren't you her grandmother?

21:33.166 --> 21:34.501
Aren't you her uncle?

21:34.584 --> 21:37.296
I knew something was up
when you refused to give her any croaker.

21:37.379 --> 21:39.131
What do croakers have to do with anything?

21:39.214 --> 21:40.716
She'd be his second wife!

21:41.508 --> 21:43.176
-He's 30 years old!
-[sighs]

21:43.260 --> 21:45.721
[Gwan-sik] Why would you give Ae-sun
to a man like him?

21:45.804 --> 21:48.765
Even if Shin Seong-il himself proposed,
he wouldn't be good enough!

21:48.849 --> 21:51.059
Shin Seong-il would never take her,
that's why.

21:51.143 --> 21:53.603
How come everyone is trying
to throw her out…

21:53.687 --> 21:55.480
[Gwan-sik sobbing]

21:56.189 --> 21:57.607
[whimpers, sobs]

21:57.691 --> 22:00.444
…when she's so smart, speaks so well,

22:00.527 --> 22:02.112
looks so beautiful?

22:03.071 --> 22:04.072
Why?

22:04.656 --> 22:05.657
Why? Why?

22:06.783 --> 22:07.951
Yell a bit louder.

22:08.910 --> 22:10.120
[frustrated groan]

22:13.957 --> 22:15.667
Let us stay together.

22:15.751 --> 22:19.921
I've been giving her fish for years
and selling her cabbages all this time.

22:20.005 --> 22:22.799
You know I love Ae-sun
more than anyone else in the world.

22:23.300 --> 22:25.802
So much more than you,
so why can't I have her?

22:25.886 --> 22:27.846
[Ae-sun's uncle]
What am I supposed to do about it?

22:27.929 --> 22:30.766
You want me to tie her up or what?
Should I put a yolk on her?

22:30.849 --> 22:33.310
Should I force her
to marry you, Yang Gwan-sik?

22:33.393 --> 22:35.479
She says she doesn't want you.
Her mind's made up!

22:35.562 --> 22:39.775
When a cow decides to rebel,
no matter what you try to do to force it,

22:40.609 --> 22:42.444
you can never make it plow again.

22:43.111 --> 22:44.988
What's wrong… what's wrong with her?

22:45.072 --> 22:46.656
Ask your mother about that.

22:47.741 --> 22:49.743
She convinced her not to marry you.

22:52.079 --> 22:54.498
So, in Busan, were you

22:54.998 --> 22:56.708
caught the day you arrived?

22:56.792 --> 22:58.627
Or did you spend the night together?

22:59.628 --> 23:01.755
These days,
couples do all kinds of things,

23:01.838 --> 23:03.715
even if they don't
spend the night together.

23:04.216 --> 23:05.592
What about you, Captain?

23:07.636 --> 23:09.679
With your first wife,
was it you who left her,

23:09.763 --> 23:12.015
or did you… or did you
get tired of each other?

23:13.600 --> 23:14.643
[scoffs]

23:17.062 --> 23:19.272
-You've got some attitude, huh?
-Yes.

23:19.815 --> 23:20.774
Yes, I do.

23:21.400 --> 23:23.902
And I don't appreciate
being addressed that way.

23:23.985 --> 23:25.654
Does that boy know this side of you?

23:26.154 --> 23:28.240
-Would he still like you?
-That's why he likes me.

23:28.323 --> 23:29.741
-[scoffs]
-[footsteps approaching]

23:29.825 --> 23:31.118
[Ae-sun's uncle] Hey, kid!

23:31.618 --> 23:33.495
Get back here before you ruin someone's--

23:33.578 --> 23:34.579
Too late.

23:34.663 --> 23:35.747
It's a party now.

23:38.458 --> 23:40.752
-Uh…
-Hold on. Stop right there.

23:40.836 --> 23:42.295
What do you want?

23:42.379 --> 23:43.839
-What now?
-Let's go.

23:46.049 --> 23:47.050
I said let's go.

23:48.218 --> 23:50.679
Where? Where are we going?

23:51.263 --> 23:52.222
Where could we go?

23:53.849 --> 23:55.600
Listen here, you little punk!

23:56.560 --> 23:59.646
This is no way to behave in front
of adults, you snot-nosed, rude--

23:59.729 --> 24:01.314
Nobody asked you, okay?

24:08.488 --> 24:11.450
Don't go. Marry me.
Take this ring, and it's a done deal.

24:12.534 --> 24:14.536
What deal? Can we live off this ring?

24:14.619 --> 24:16.872
Are we running away again?
Becoming thieves?

24:16.955 --> 24:18.957
Are you really gonna marry this guy?

24:20.792 --> 24:22.752
Why would you? I don't get it.

24:22.836 --> 24:24.337
It's a second marriage.

24:24.963 --> 24:25.797
He has two kids.

24:26.882 --> 24:29.301
I don't get why. Tell me why.

24:29.384 --> 24:31.970
You're right. Why's it me?
Why always Ae-sun?

24:32.053 --> 24:34.639
Why do I get the blame?
Why was I expelled?

24:34.723 --> 24:36.516
Why does everybody think I'm the worst?

24:36.600 --> 24:37.684
[tender piano music playing]

24:37.767 --> 24:39.352
It's gone to crap. Poetry?

24:39.936 --> 24:40.770
College?

24:41.438 --> 24:43.815
Right. Now, that's all over.

24:44.816 --> 24:46.902
I can't make a living
with no high school degree.

24:46.985 --> 24:48.320
I said I'll take care of you.

24:48.403 --> 24:50.405
-No matter what, I'll find a way.
-How exactly?

24:51.114 --> 24:53.492
What have you done for me
except follow me around everywhere

24:53.575 --> 24:55.911
and toss me an old fish
every now and then?

24:55.994 --> 24:57.913
-I'm not a beggar!
-You were just ten years old.

24:57.996 --> 24:59.706
We were just little kids.

24:59.789 --> 25:00.957
We were children.

25:01.625 --> 25:04.294
He can provide,
and he can send me to college.

25:04.377 --> 25:06.213
-He'll let me be a poet.
-I can do that!

25:06.296 --> 25:08.381
I'll work on boats. I'll lay down bricks.

25:08.465 --> 25:10.967
-I'll do anything!
-No, I don't want you! I don't!

25:12.010 --> 25:13.386
[grunts]

25:14.262 --> 25:16.014
[breathing shakily]

25:19.768 --> 25:20.852
If we get married,

25:21.645 --> 25:23.688
the last chance I have will be over.

25:26.733 --> 25:27.567
What?

25:28.151 --> 25:30.195
I'm tired of having to fight
every single day,

25:30.278 --> 25:33.281
of sticking up for myself,
living with a family that doesn't want me.

25:33.949 --> 25:34.908
I want to be rich.

25:35.909 --> 25:37.369
I want to be comfortable.

25:37.452 --> 25:40.372
And if I marry you,
I… I'll just face more abuse.

25:40.455 --> 25:41.790
They all know what I've been.

25:42.290 --> 25:44.709
But if I marry him, I'll finally be free.

25:44.793 --> 25:48.338
Free from you, Gwan-sik,
'cause you know… know me and everything.

25:48.421 --> 25:49.381
I feel so…

25:51.258 --> 25:52.676
[sobs]

25:54.928 --> 25:56.680
…so ashamed.

25:58.640 --> 26:00.892
I've been living in shame my whole life.

26:01.393 --> 26:03.311
[young Gwan-sik]
There's an extra one for free.

26:03.395 --> 26:06.231
[man] Did your mom say that?
Well, did she?

26:06.314 --> 26:07.983
You have six people in your family,

26:08.066 --> 26:09.818
but for some reason, you only buy five.

26:09.901 --> 26:12.237
[man] Think you're rich enough
to give them away, is that it?

26:12.320 --> 26:13.280
Mind your own business.

26:14.739 --> 26:16.658
Damn that little runt.

26:19.244 --> 26:21.204
[young Ae-sun] You saw it all. [sobs]

26:22.372 --> 26:23.873
Oh, Mom.

26:23.957 --> 26:26.626
Oh, Mom, I miss you so much.

26:27.335 --> 26:29.087
[Ae-sun] Go to Busan, he said.

26:30.005 --> 26:32.048
He told me to go work at a factory.

26:32.841 --> 26:34.759
I don't have a home anymore.

26:34.843 --> 26:36.344
[Ae-sun sobs]

26:36.428 --> 26:40.265
[Ae-sun] You know everything about me.
Do you want me trapped in it forever?

26:43.351 --> 26:44.561
If you stay here…

26:46.688 --> 26:49.024
I'll never be happy, married or not.

26:50.191 --> 26:52.527
If you care about me, let me live my life.

26:52.611 --> 26:54.613
[music fades]

26:57.282 --> 26:58.950
Let me live without you.

27:03.288 --> 27:04.331
Are you saying

27:05.081 --> 27:06.583
that I'm in your way, Ae-sun?

27:13.798 --> 27:14.674
Gwan-sik.

27:17.344 --> 27:19.304
Gwan-sik, this is what needs to happen.

27:20.764 --> 27:22.349
If you want me to live my life…

27:24.476 --> 27:25.685
you have to leave.

27:26.978 --> 27:29.189
[melancholy string music playing]

27:36.529 --> 27:37.739
[Gwan-sik sobs]

27:46.081 --> 27:47.165
[Ae-sun's daughter] At 18,

27:47.248 --> 27:49.584
she stared into
the eyes of her first love,

27:49.668 --> 27:51.836
knowing she may never see him again.

27:51.920 --> 27:54.005
[music soars]

27:54.089 --> 27:57.717
She buried that pure love
in the yellow field of spring

27:58.593 --> 28:00.345
and broke her own dreams.

28:00.428 --> 28:02.305
[sobs] My ring.

28:06.184 --> 28:08.687
[crying]

28:08.770 --> 28:10.563
My ring.

28:16.945 --> 28:18.446
[music fades]

28:21.533 --> 28:25.245
They say that working a field
is more rewarding than parenting a child.

28:26.413 --> 28:27.997
You sure never tried it with me, Ae-sun.

28:28.081 --> 28:30.667
Nothing special
for your little sister-in-law.

28:31.501 --> 28:34.087
When she splits the eggs,
she always gives you the bigger one.

28:34.671 --> 28:36.005
Like, every single time.

28:36.089 --> 28:37.465
There you go again with that talk.

28:37.549 --> 28:40.301
Mom, why'd you marry
into a family like this anyway?

28:40.844 --> 28:43.263
I chose my own path, dear. Nobody else.

28:44.180 --> 28:46.349
I'd never decide to live like you did.

28:46.975 --> 28:48.768
Like, never. Never.

28:49.686 --> 28:53.022
I'm going to marry a man from Seoul
for sure, no matter what.

28:53.106 --> 28:57.318
I'd never marry a man who doesn't know
what "nostalgia" is. Never!

28:57.402 --> 28:58.361
[chuckles]

28:59.028 --> 29:02.699
Well, you know what they say,
"Never say never," eh?

29:03.241 --> 29:04.451
[wistful music playing]

29:04.534 --> 29:07.203
Honestly, don't you regret it a little?

29:09.330 --> 29:10.832
No, of course not.

29:10.915 --> 29:14.127
If I hadn't met your father,
I wouldn't have any of you.

29:14.210 --> 29:15.754
Come on. Not as our mother.

29:15.837 --> 29:16.921
As Oh Ae-sun.

29:20.508 --> 29:21.509
Eat your chicken.

29:21.593 --> 29:23.303
What? Say something.

29:24.095 --> 29:25.555
Would Oh Ae-sun regret it?

29:26.139 --> 29:28.850
Do you ever think about
what could have been?

29:29.768 --> 29:30.852
Oh Ae-sun.

29:30.935 --> 29:32.520
[tender piano music playing]

29:32.604 --> 29:34.314
If you really want to know…

29:37.567 --> 29:39.569
she was forever broken that spring.

29:40.069 --> 29:42.113
[ship horn blares]

29:42.197 --> 29:44.199
[people cheering]

29:48.453 --> 29:51.164
-[cheering continues]
-[indistinct shouting]

30:04.260 --> 30:08.264
[indistinct chattering]

30:10.475 --> 30:11.601
[patron] Oh, it's perfect.

30:12.352 --> 30:13.978
The handle is really…

30:14.062 --> 30:15.605
Oh my goodness.

30:15.688 --> 30:18.650
Kids, don't touch them. They'll die, okay?

30:18.733 --> 30:22.529
Give us some good ones.
Don't use up the leftovers on the locals.

30:24.823 --> 30:28.159
Gwang-rye,
will you please stop crying already?

30:29.452 --> 30:32.413
Look at you there.
You're sending away your precious son.

30:32.497 --> 30:35.834
May he get to shore and find himself
a wife from a noble family.

30:37.085 --> 30:38.211
[Gye-ok scoffs]

30:40.129 --> 30:43.174
[Mak-cheon] So we tried it your way
and fed worms to the chicken.

30:43.258 --> 30:46.302
I'm impressed, my dear.
I really am. You did great.

30:46.803 --> 30:48.721
I'm a bit frightened of you too.

30:52.141 --> 30:53.268
[Ae-sun] Mrs. Yang?

30:53.893 --> 30:57.188
I wanted to ask you something, if I could?

31:00.733 --> 31:01.901
Go ahead.

31:01.985 --> 31:04.696
You can talk to me
like you would with your own mother.

31:06.114 --> 31:08.449
Uh, is it true

31:09.409 --> 31:13.204
that Gwan-sik is one of
the fastest four runners on Jeju Island?

31:14.163 --> 31:17.083
Is he… is he really
that close to winning medals?

31:18.668 --> 31:22.255
I think if he could focus on it,
he probably could've won medals, yes.

31:22.338 --> 31:25.466
He's not even really in fourth place.
He's practically third.

31:26.050 --> 31:28.678
Honestly, it's pretty much neck and neck.

31:29.596 --> 31:31.848
What a total and utter idiot.

31:31.931 --> 31:35.226
Uh, do you guys usually
talk to each other that way?

31:35.310 --> 31:38.104
He said he was only
in athletics for the food.

31:38.688 --> 31:40.648
He never said he was actually good.

31:40.732 --> 31:41.733
[sobs]

31:41.816 --> 31:45.778
How can he follow me around for ten years
without telling me he likes athletics?

31:46.529 --> 31:49.741
He always lets me go on and on
about becoming a poet, while he…

31:50.992 --> 31:51.951
while he…

31:52.035 --> 31:54.454
Boys from the Yang family are like that.

31:54.537 --> 31:58.541
Because they always assume
they shouldn't express their own opinions.

31:58.625 --> 31:59.751
[sighs]

32:03.922 --> 32:06.257
[breathes deeply]

32:06.799 --> 32:07.884
Ae-sun.

32:09.761 --> 32:10.803
Gwan-sik…

32:14.057 --> 32:16.184
will lose everything if he stays with you.

32:16.267 --> 32:19.479
He will lose his dreams
as well as his family.

32:21.022 --> 32:23.399
You know what it means to be lonely,
don't you?

32:23.900 --> 32:24.734
Huh?

32:24.817 --> 32:26.569
[tender piano music playing]

32:26.653 --> 32:28.988
Don't take this away from Gwan-sik.

32:29.489 --> 32:32.951
Let him live his life
to its fullest potential.

32:35.286 --> 32:36.412
Ae-sun.

32:40.583 --> 32:42.377
Let him live his life,

32:42.961 --> 32:43.795
okay?

32:45.672 --> 32:46.631
Are you saying…

32:49.300 --> 32:50.969
I'm standing in his way?

32:52.553 --> 32:53.388
Are you saying…

32:55.139 --> 32:56.599
that I'm in your way, Ae-sun?

32:57.725 --> 32:59.394
[ship horn blares]

32:59.477 --> 33:01.479
[bells dinging]

33:03.064 --> 33:04.273
[passenger] I love you!

33:09.696 --> 33:11.072
I love you!

33:11.155 --> 33:13.658
-[hissing]
-[ship horn blaring]

33:15.910 --> 33:18.079
[cheering]

33:30.425 --> 33:31.342
[coach] Gwan-sik!

33:32.468 --> 33:33.469
Here.

33:34.512 --> 33:36.139
Oh, don't look so down.

33:36.222 --> 33:38.141
I've been coaching for ten years,

33:38.224 --> 33:41.269
and none of my students ever ran
a hundred laps 'cause I told 'em to.

33:41.352 --> 33:43.354
You're the first one to take me up on it.

33:43.438 --> 33:46.858
Your mother is going to sell fish
so you can go study on the mainland.

33:46.941 --> 33:49.652
So let's train hard
and win a gold medal for her, eh?

33:50.153 --> 33:51.571
Once you win a gold medal,

33:52.780 --> 33:55.033
you'll forget all about that girl.

33:55.992 --> 33:57.160
You know that gold medals…

33:57.243 --> 33:58.286
Yeah?

33:58.369 --> 33:59.412
…aren't pure gold?

34:01.330 --> 34:02.165
Huh?

34:04.208 --> 34:07.211
Why should I work so hard
for something that's not pure gold?

34:07.712 --> 34:08.963
I don't need one anymore.

34:09.047 --> 34:10.506
What, is your life over?

34:10.590 --> 34:13.801
You've been going on and on about
going to the mainland and winning gold.

34:13.885 --> 34:15.344
I said that 'cause…

34:16.721 --> 34:18.681
because Ae-sun wanted to leave the island.

34:18.765 --> 34:22.268
Are you telling me
your only purpose in life is this Ae-sun?

34:22.351 --> 34:23.352
That's right.

34:24.479 --> 34:25.521
Come on, get up. Get up!

34:25.605 --> 34:28.900
The hundred laps,
I… I only ran them because of Ae-sun.

34:30.276 --> 34:33.112
I can't get to Seoul selling fish.
School grades aren't good enough.

34:33.196 --> 34:35.406
So I thought being good at sports
was my only shot.

34:35.490 --> 34:36.866
Who wants to do that?

34:38.534 --> 34:41.079
-Come on, stand up.
-I actually hate athletics.

34:42.330 --> 34:43.414
And that's the truth.

34:43.498 --> 34:45.208
-What?
-I'm not cut out for it.

34:45.291 --> 34:48.169
They could give me a box of gold.
I'll never finish above fourth.

34:50.755 --> 34:52.215
Without her, I wouldn't have done it.

34:52.298 --> 34:53.466
[gasps]

34:53.549 --> 34:57.011
You crazy bastard.
Then why are you going to Seoul right now?

34:59.055 --> 35:00.973
[Ae-sun] Gwan-sik,
this is what needs to happen.

35:01.974 --> 35:03.559
If you want me to live my life,

35:04.936 --> 35:06.354
you have to leave.

35:06.437 --> 35:07.772
[ethereal music playing]

35:09.357 --> 35:13.069
[clock ticking]

35:14.570 --> 35:15.738
[music fades]

35:18.449 --> 35:21.327
[ticking fades]

35:23.538 --> 35:25.206
I'm a modern man, you know?

35:27.917 --> 35:29.293
I'm willing to forgive you.

35:31.087 --> 35:33.631
Any other family
would've shown you the door.

35:37.677 --> 35:40.346
How dare that boy speak to me that way?
He's a nobody.

35:40.429 --> 35:41.722
God!

35:42.515 --> 35:45.560
When all his family does
is run a tiny little fishmonger?

35:46.185 --> 35:49.272
He doesn't even own anything,
that impudent little punk.

35:49.355 --> 35:51.149
The store isn't that tiny.

35:51.774 --> 35:54.986
-What?
-I said it isn't that tiny. His store.

35:55.069 --> 35:57.488
Well, well,
you think just because I'm nice to you,

35:57.572 --> 35:59.615
that gives you the right
to speak to an adult that way?

35:59.699 --> 36:01.784
Then why is an adult marrying a child?

36:01.868 --> 36:04.120
[chuckles] Listen, you brat.

36:04.203 --> 36:06.789
-Don't speak rudely to me.
-Watch yourself.

36:07.623 --> 36:10.543
I'm really starting to think you don't
fully appreciate your situation here.

36:10.626 --> 36:13.796
I can't speak my mind to a girl
whose tuition I'm going to pay?

36:13.880 --> 36:16.716
It's not like I'm marrying
the virgin daughter of a wealthy family.

36:16.799 --> 36:18.384
Keep your damn money, then.

36:19.510 --> 36:20.428
I don't want it.

36:22.763 --> 36:23.806
Really?

36:25.308 --> 36:27.059
Wait, wait, are you… serious?

36:28.519 --> 36:30.438
[Ae-sun sobs] What about college?

36:30.521 --> 36:33.900
What about being a poet in the mainland?

36:33.983 --> 36:35.985
[emotional piano music playing]

36:37.153 --> 36:40.072
Well, I think that…
that my family should pay for me to go.

36:45.703 --> 36:49.415
Hold on now. I… I thought that
you were marrying me to go to college.

36:50.249 --> 36:51.751
Why else would you marry me?

36:54.003 --> 36:55.838
I said, why else would you marry me?

36:57.590 --> 36:58.758
'Cause I don't

37:00.384 --> 37:01.510
have anywhere else.

37:03.721 --> 37:04.555
What?

37:06.849 --> 37:08.768
'Cause there's nothing else I can do.

37:09.936 --> 37:11.562
[young Ae-sun] I'm going to do it all.

37:11.646 --> 37:14.565
[laughs] And I mean all of it.

37:14.649 --> 37:16.692
I'm going to be the chief
of the fishing village,

37:16.776 --> 37:18.819
and then I'll be president
five times in a row.

37:18.903 --> 37:21.781
-[laughter]
-All right. Go on, do it!

37:21.864 --> 37:24.450
This country could use
a haenyeo president for once.

37:24.951 --> 37:27.703
I can't believe that she wasn't a boy.

37:28.204 --> 37:30.498
How can a girl
with such a tiny little face

37:30.581 --> 37:33.334
have such giant potential? You tell me.

37:33.417 --> 37:36.170
If she has such talent,
what choice does she have?

37:36.254 --> 37:38.297
-She'll have to be president.
-[laughs]

37:38.381 --> 37:40.925
Go ahead.
You already have eight votes from us.

37:41.509 --> 37:42.593
[laughs]

37:42.677 --> 37:44.011
[young Gwan-sik] Nine votes.

37:45.554 --> 37:47.098
[woman 6] That's right. Nine votes.

37:47.890 --> 37:49.475
What grade did you get in math?

37:51.227 --> 37:52.728
When you grow up, what will you be?

37:54.438 --> 37:55.356
[sniffles]

37:56.482 --> 37:58.067
What are you asking him for?

37:59.443 --> 38:01.153
[young Gwan-sik] The First Gentleman.

38:03.823 --> 38:04.949
The First Gentleman.

38:05.032 --> 38:07.201
[laughter]

38:07.827 --> 38:09.537
What did he say? [laughs]

38:09.620 --> 38:10.538
Goodness.

38:10.621 --> 38:11.747
Oh, stop it.

38:11.831 --> 38:12.915
[woman 4] Too much.

38:13.416 --> 38:14.583
[woman 3] Aw.

38:15.501 --> 38:17.128
[woman 5] So cute together.

38:17.211 --> 38:19.213
[emotional piano music continues]

38:19.297 --> 38:22.633
[clock ticking]

38:25.720 --> 38:26.971
[breathes anxiously]

38:27.763 --> 38:30.850
The truth is, I'm getting married
because I have nowhere else.

38:31.684 --> 38:33.686
I have nowhere to go. I can just die.

38:33.769 --> 38:37.315
But they say you're better off living
on a pile of dog crap than dead.

38:37.398 --> 38:38.649
I'm the pile of dog crap?

38:39.275 --> 38:41.986
Hey, can't you just hire me or something?

38:42.069 --> 38:44.280
I'll be a housekeeper.
I'm worth it, I swear.

38:44.363 --> 38:45.323
[laughing]

38:47.325 --> 38:48.200
[scoffs]

38:48.284 --> 38:50.494
Look, if I'm getting married,

38:50.578 --> 38:52.705
I'm already getting
a housekeeper for free.

38:53.372 --> 38:54.832
Why would I hire you?

38:55.499 --> 38:56.917
You may be the queen of love,

38:57.001 --> 38:59.045
but not everyone dreams about
marrying their soulmate.

38:59.128 --> 39:00.338
I just want a normal wife.

39:00.421 --> 39:03.758
I want a humble daughter-in-law
and a frugal mother to my children.

39:04.800 --> 39:05.676
Jeez.

39:10.139 --> 39:13.809
You know what? I only met my ex-wife
five times before we got married.

39:14.393 --> 39:15.728
That's how a lot of people do it.

39:15.811 --> 39:17.813
Why are you making this such a big deal?

39:17.897 --> 39:18.731
God.

39:19.982 --> 39:21.442
You know what? Stop.

39:21.525 --> 39:23.027
Just give us the cheapest one.

39:25.988 --> 39:28.491
[clock chiming]

39:34.121 --> 39:36.415
Now, I want you to tell me the truth.

39:37.958 --> 39:40.002
You slept with him, didn't you, Ae-sun?

39:40.086 --> 39:42.088
[emotional music playing]

39:48.761 --> 39:51.305
[crying]

39:53.974 --> 39:55.810
Good riddance, you crazy brat, you.

39:57.478 --> 39:59.480
[Ae-sun's daughter]
If she hadn't run that day…

40:00.314 --> 40:01.816
if she hadn't run…

40:01.899 --> 40:03.067
[ship horn blares]

40:03.150 --> 40:04.652
[Gye-ok] Come on, Gyeong-ok.

40:04.735 --> 40:05.778
Let's go home.

40:08.364 --> 40:11.492
[ship horn blaring]

40:11.575 --> 40:13.869
[woman 5] It's raining cats and dogs.

40:15.454 --> 40:17.706
Thank goodness this trouble is over.

40:18.374 --> 40:21.085
Their feelings will fade with distance.
Mark my words.

40:21.168 --> 40:23.087
Yeah, you know what they say.

40:23.587 --> 40:25.923
Once a broken heart,
always a broken heart.

40:26.006 --> 40:27.425
That's what they say at least.

40:27.508 --> 40:28.717
[Ae-sun] Gwan-sik!

40:30.219 --> 40:31.387
Gwan-sik!

40:33.013 --> 40:34.598
Gwan-sik!

40:34.682 --> 40:36.976
[emotional music continues]

40:37.059 --> 40:38.936
[Ae-sun] Where are you going?

40:39.019 --> 40:40.688
[crying]

40:40.771 --> 40:42.106
Don't leave me!

40:43.691 --> 40:46.360
Please don't leave me here alone!

40:47.278 --> 40:49.029
-Oh dear.
-[Ae-sun] Gwan-sik!

40:49.113 --> 40:51.073
What could be stronger than young love?

40:51.157 --> 40:52.825
[Ae-sun] Yang Gwan-sik!

40:53.451 --> 40:54.785
Yang Gwan-sik!

40:54.869 --> 40:56.871
[ship horn blares]

40:56.954 --> 40:58.914
Hey, Yang Gwan-sik!

40:58.998 --> 41:00.291
[pants, sobs]

41:00.374 --> 41:02.960
-[ship horn blares]
-[coach] Wow, that sure is loud!

41:05.880 --> 41:07.298
[ship horn blares]

41:07.381 --> 41:09.258
[passenger] Ae-sun. [echoes]

41:11.302 --> 41:12.636
Ae-sun.

41:12.720 --> 41:14.138
Careful, you're gonna fall.

41:14.638 --> 41:16.140
Come on up. [groans]

41:16.223 --> 41:17.933
My baby.

41:21.896 --> 41:23.856
[loud clang]

41:24.440 --> 41:25.441
[thud echoes]

41:25.524 --> 41:27.776
[ship horn blares]

41:27.860 --> 41:29.695
[high-pitched tone]

41:29.778 --> 41:31.697
[Ae-sun muffled] Yang Gwan-sik!

41:32.781 --> 41:35.367
Yang Gwan-sik! [sobs]

41:35.451 --> 41:37.786
[ship horn blares]

41:37.870 --> 41:39.830
[Ae-sun] Yang Gwan-sik!

41:40.414 --> 41:43.417
[melodic music playing]

41:46.128 --> 41:47.254
Yang Gwan-sik!

41:47.922 --> 41:49.423
Yang Gwan-sik!

41:51.050 --> 41:52.510
Yang Gwan-sik!

41:55.596 --> 41:56.847
[Ae-sun sobs]

41:58.098 --> 42:00.017
Please don't go!

42:02.102 --> 42:03.521
Don't go!

42:06.857 --> 42:08.108
[crying]

42:13.656 --> 42:16.116
[crying continues]

42:16.200 --> 42:18.244
My goodness. That crazy brat.

42:19.036 --> 42:22.289
-Hey, don't you have a heart?
-Mind your own business, woman!

42:22.373 --> 42:23.415
[grunts angrily]

42:23.499 --> 42:26.585
Leave her alone.
Let her scream if she wants.

42:26.669 --> 42:28.671
[Ae-sun crying]

42:35.427 --> 42:37.680
Why do you take everything away?

42:39.139 --> 42:41.642
Why do you take everything away?

42:41.725 --> 42:43.727
[crying continues]

42:47.523 --> 42:49.191
Oh, Mom!

42:51.318 --> 42:53.153
Mom!

42:53.654 --> 42:55.656
[melodic music continues]

43:00.995 --> 43:03.622
-[wind gusting]
-[rain pattering]

43:03.706 --> 43:04.873
Ah.

43:05.374 --> 43:06.709
What's going on?

43:06.792 --> 43:08.627
Is someone kicking the Dragon King?

43:08.711 --> 43:10.504
Why are the winds so strong
all of a sudden?

43:10.588 --> 43:12.881
Ah. Hey!

43:14.133 --> 43:15.593
We got some headwinds, everyone.

43:15.676 --> 43:17.803
Turn this boat around!
You have to turn it around!

43:17.886 --> 43:19.805
-[coach] We're at sea!
-Turn this boat around!

43:19.888 --> 43:21.181
Please turn it around!

43:21.265 --> 43:23.601
-You've got to turn it around. Sir!
-[coach] Come on, kid!

43:23.684 --> 43:24.768
[man] Get out of here!

43:24.852 --> 43:27.521
Sir, please! Please turn the boat around!

43:27.605 --> 43:28.897
-I'm begging you!
-Get out!

43:28.981 --> 43:31.442
-Please! It'll just be a second!
-[coach] You're crazy!

43:31.525 --> 43:34.445
Let me go! Turn it around, please!

43:34.528 --> 43:37.114
Why is that little crazy lunatic
on my boat again?

43:37.906 --> 43:40.034
Please, Captain, please!
You have to turn it around!

43:40.117 --> 43:40.951
[coach grunts]

43:41.035 --> 43:43.120
-Please, I have to go back!
-Gwan-sik!

43:44.371 --> 43:45.664
Are you insane?

43:45.748 --> 43:48.250
You think you're gonna die
without her or what?

43:49.585 --> 43:51.587
[thunder rumbling]

43:54.423 --> 43:55.924
[emotional string music playing]

43:56.008 --> 43:59.303
[Ae-sun's daughter]
That day, if she hadn't run…

44:00.721 --> 44:01.847
[Ae-sun crying]

44:01.930 --> 44:03.807
…if she hadn't run…

44:03.891 --> 44:05.726
[woman 6] You're destroying those kids.

44:05.809 --> 44:08.520
Don't you remember
what happened to Romeo and Juliet?

44:09.229 --> 44:11.482
People don't die from broken hearts.

44:12.608 --> 44:15.903
Once the boat leaves,
they're in the hands of the Dragon King.

44:15.986 --> 44:17.988
There's nothing else we can do for them.

44:18.739 --> 44:19.657
Let's go.

44:20.366 --> 44:23.243
Ae-sun, come on.
I'll make you something with pork.

44:23.327 --> 44:25.412
Pork is better than boys, sometimes.

44:26.205 --> 44:27.039
Oh my.

44:27.122 --> 44:29.291
[music soars]

44:30.042 --> 44:32.002
[Ae-sun's daughter]
If she hadn't run that day…

44:32.086 --> 44:34.213
Is that the signal for a man overboard?

44:34.797 --> 44:36.548
Did… did someone go over the side?

44:36.632 --> 44:37.841
Hey, Ma.

44:38.592 --> 44:40.678
-He jumped. He jumped in the ocean.
-What?

44:41.345 --> 44:42.262
He jumped.

44:42.346 --> 44:44.765
-He just jumped in the ocean.
-Hmm?

44:48.894 --> 44:50.938
So people don't die from broken hearts?

44:51.021 --> 44:54.608
If he has so much going for him,
why would he jump off the side?

44:55.359 --> 44:57.528
-[Mak-cheon groans]
-[Gye-ok] Oh no. Mom! Oh no!

44:57.611 --> 44:58.445
Hey.

44:59.988 --> 45:01.990
[breathing shakily]

45:06.829 --> 45:08.038
[Ae-sun's daughter] That day,

45:08.914 --> 45:12.209
if she hadn't run as fast as she could…

45:12.710 --> 45:13.544
Oh!

45:15.087 --> 45:17.464
Look at him. What is he, a whale?

45:18.507 --> 45:20.217
How in the world can he swim like that?

45:25.806 --> 45:27.599
[Ae-sun's daughter]
If she hadn't run that day…

45:27.683 --> 45:29.017
[upbeat pop music playing]

45:29.101 --> 45:32.396
…would she have been able
to outrun her destiny?

45:32.479 --> 45:34.940
[breathing heavily]

45:43.449 --> 45:44.992
U-turn!

45:45.075 --> 45:45.951
U-turn!

45:46.034 --> 45:48.704
[all cheering]

45:48.787 --> 45:49.705
Let's go!

45:49.788 --> 45:52.082
-U-turn, Gwan-sik!
-That's my boy. Let's go!

45:54.752 --> 45:57.629
Go, go, go, go!

45:59.757 --> 46:01.467
[panting, gasping]

46:04.553 --> 46:06.096
[cheering]

46:06.722 --> 46:09.183
You fool! Why did you teach him to swim?

46:09.266 --> 46:11.059
[woman 5 laughs]

46:11.143 --> 46:14.271
Let's send the boy to the North as a spy!

46:14.354 --> 46:16.356
[upbeat pop music continues]

46:20.736 --> 46:22.362
[Ae-sun's daughter] But in the end,

46:22.446 --> 46:24.656
destiny was a stubborn thing.

46:42.800 --> 46:44.384
[breathing anxiously]

46:52.726 --> 46:54.728
[both panting]

46:55.521 --> 46:57.648
[Ae-sun sobs happily]

46:57.731 --> 46:58.982
Oh! Oh!

46:59.066 --> 47:00.526
Oh my goodness!

47:06.657 --> 47:07.616
Are you okay?

47:09.201 --> 47:11.203
[Ae-sun sobbing]

47:14.623 --> 47:15.749
[music stops]

47:15.833 --> 47:17.584
I have to pay for this outfit.

47:18.877 --> 47:19.795
I have money.

47:20.504 --> 47:21.630
I have money.

47:24.299 --> 47:25.133
What did he say?

47:25.217 --> 47:26.051
I don't know.

47:26.677 --> 47:28.846
He just eats sugar cubes all day.

47:29.972 --> 47:31.515
[both sob]

47:31.598 --> 47:33.559
[upbeat pop music resumes]

47:44.945 --> 47:48.407
Have you ever seen anything like that?
I mean, just look at that.

47:50.784 --> 47:53.287
This is even better than Romeo and Juliet.

47:55.998 --> 47:58.375
Well, you know
that there are certain things

47:58.458 --> 48:00.252
the heavens up there above us

48:00.335 --> 48:02.880
can't possibly stop from unfolding
either way, Gye-ok.

48:04.089 --> 48:06.341
And then,
when the day of fate finally arrives,

48:06.425 --> 48:08.385
it's better to just get out of the way.

48:08.969 --> 48:11.305
[woman 6] Looks like
neither family could stop it.

48:12.598 --> 48:14.725
There's no reward for parenting, is there?

48:20.230 --> 48:21.398
[Gye-ok sighs]

48:23.150 --> 48:24.359
[sniffles]

48:24.443 --> 48:26.069
-[music ends]
-[sniffles]

48:30.032 --> 48:31.533
Hey, you wanna know something?

48:32.784 --> 48:34.369
Your parents ran away as kids.

48:36.079 --> 48:37.456
Is that true, Mom?

48:38.081 --> 48:40.250
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
Your auntie is drunk again.

48:40.876 --> 48:42.753
Those two caused such a ruckus

48:42.836 --> 48:45.923
that all of the seas between Jeju
and Busan were shaken by it.

48:46.006 --> 48:48.258
You're drunk
and confusing me with your mom.

48:48.342 --> 48:50.886
That was her. I never ran away anywhere.

48:50.969 --> 48:52.679
But it's funny, isn't it?

48:52.763 --> 48:54.348
What happened in Busan?

48:55.349 --> 48:57.601
That's it, you're going home.
Come on, get up.

48:57.684 --> 48:58.852
What happened?

48:58.936 --> 49:00.979
It only took two days
for them to get caught.

49:01.063 --> 49:02.773
-[middle-aged Ae-sun] Stop it!
-Just think.

49:02.856 --> 49:06.568
All right, drink some water.
Let's get you sobered up, all right?

49:07.194 --> 49:08.362
There we are.

49:08.445 --> 49:10.822
Hey, hey, can you call her husband
to come pick her up?

49:11.490 --> 49:14.660
I just said that Busan is a fertile land.
You were such a gift.

49:14.743 --> 49:18.497
Gyeong-ok, I'm going to call
your husband here, all right? Come on.

49:18.580 --> 49:20.999
You're the reason
they moved out, you know.

49:22.334 --> 49:24.670
You were born eight months
after the wedding,

49:24.753 --> 49:27.464
even though they were caught
in only two days. [laughs]

49:28.799 --> 49:31.176
Like I said, Busan is a fertile land.

49:31.259 --> 49:32.678
You were a gift.

49:34.096 --> 49:36.723
Clearly, you were conceived in Busan,
not in Jeju.

49:36.807 --> 49:39.017
[middle-aged Ae-sun sighs]

49:39.101 --> 49:41.103
[Gyeong-ok] It was spring, wasn't it?
It was spring.

49:42.562 --> 49:44.564
Spring has a way with people.

49:45.607 --> 49:47.567
[Ae-sun's daughter] Spring on Jeju Island

49:48.235 --> 49:49.778
is always too short

49:50.737 --> 49:52.614
but never lacking in spirit.

49:55.742 --> 49:57.494
[slurred] I think we should have,

49:58.245 --> 49:59.371
like, uh,

49:59.871 --> 50:01.289
three babies?

50:01.373 --> 50:03.166
I think three would be perfect.

50:03.250 --> 50:06.670
So, if we're going to pay,

50:06.753 --> 50:08.839
listen, pay for their education,

50:08.922 --> 50:12.467
we need to do this strategically
and plan how we live.

50:13.176 --> 50:14.011
Mm.

50:14.511 --> 50:16.263
Like General MacArthur?

50:17.097 --> 50:19.349
So, strategically,

50:20.058 --> 50:22.519
we should try to have a daughter first.

50:22.602 --> 50:24.396
And then a son, and then…

50:24.479 --> 50:25.689
We don't have time.

50:26.273 --> 50:27.107
Huh?

50:31.028 --> 50:31.862
No time.

50:37.367 --> 50:39.369
[upbeat accordion music playing]

50:43.165 --> 50:45.709
[Gyeong-ok laughing]

50:45.792 --> 50:48.920
[Gyeong-ok] Were you having
a wild circus in there or what?

50:49.004 --> 50:51.882
How did you manage to break
the fan on the wall?

50:51.965 --> 50:53.633
[laughing]

50:53.717 --> 50:58.221
Even my own mother thinks that
Yang Gwan-sik and Oh Ae-sun broke the fan.

50:59.014 --> 51:01.850
[middle-aged Gwan-sik]
Hey, get out. Get out, you little brat.

51:01.933 --> 51:03.018
Get out of my house.

51:03.560 --> 51:06.938
Everybody would call you "Dia"
when she was pregnant with you

51:07.022 --> 51:09.691
because that's the brand of soju
they drank in Busan--

51:09.775 --> 51:12.652
Hey. It's time to go home. You're drunk!

51:12.736 --> 51:15.489
You're the ones who ran away,
so why take it out on me?

51:15.572 --> 51:18.909
You're the one who came into my home today
and ate all our chicken.

51:19.534 --> 51:22.037
-Go on. Go back to your house.
-[Gyeong-ok] There's chicken left.

51:22.120 --> 51:24.623
-Don't tell me to leave.
-Okay. We'll pack it for you, all right?

51:24.706 --> 51:26.708
Put on your jacket. Get out of here.

51:34.758 --> 51:37.177
-[Ae-sun] Geum-myeong. Look over here.
-[Gwan-sik laughs]

51:37.260 --> 51:39.221
[Ae-sun] One, two, three.

51:39.304 --> 51:40.806
[camera shutter clicks]

51:40.889 --> 51:43.183
[both laughing]

51:43.266 --> 51:46.269
Look at her little head.
It's so round, isn't it?

51:46.353 --> 51:48.063
[Ae-sun] Aw, look at you.

51:48.146 --> 51:50.315
Oh, how do you know
how to smile like that?

51:50.398 --> 51:51.775
-Mm.
-[Gwan-sik] Yeah

51:51.858 --> 51:53.985
-[Ae-sun] Goodness.
-Mm.

51:54.069 --> 51:55.320
-A cutie pie.
-She is.

51:56.404 --> 51:57.280
A cute little brat.

51:58.448 --> 52:00.951
A cute little brat kept Mommy at home.

52:01.034 --> 52:02.369
[Geum-myeong crying]

52:02.452 --> 52:04.996
[Gwan-sik] Okay. Aw. [chuckles]

52:05.622 --> 52:08.625
Oh, coochie-coo. Oh, come on.

52:08.708 --> 52:11.753
What's so important about college
after this beauty, hmm?

52:11.837 --> 52:15.298
I already have
the whole entire world right here.

52:15.382 --> 52:17.968
This little girl will be my inspiration.

52:18.677 --> 52:20.053
Won't you? [chuckles]

52:20.137 --> 52:21.805
Oh. Sh.

52:22.472 --> 52:24.266
[sighs] Hi.

52:24.933 --> 52:26.560
Hi. Mm.

52:27.394 --> 52:28.854
Sh.

52:30.021 --> 52:31.940
[man on radio]
…won first place in the 400 meters…

52:32.023 --> 52:33.608
[Ae-sun] Aw.

52:33.692 --> 52:37.737
The young man, named Jo O-ryeon,
seemingly appeared out of nowhere

52:37.821 --> 52:42.576
and expressed his desire to win
the gold medal at the Bangkok Asian Games.

52:43.076 --> 52:45.078
[tender acoustic guitar music playing]

52:51.543 --> 52:52.586
You're not upset?

52:53.795 --> 52:55.839
That you aren't a champion
like Jo O-ryeon?

53:00.260 --> 53:03.430
[Gwan-sik] What's a gold medal to me
when I have Geum-myeong?

53:05.182 --> 53:07.517
My only dream is this little thing.

53:07.601 --> 53:09.269
[Ae-sun chuckles]

53:09.352 --> 53:11.271
[Geum-myeong]
The springtime of their lives

53:11.771 --> 53:13.523
passed by so quickly.

53:13.982 --> 53:15.859
FLAG
THIS IS A SILENT OUTCRY

53:15.942 --> 53:20.447
By the age of 18,
Mom lost her dream and started a family.

53:22.657 --> 53:24.451
By the age of 19,

53:24.534 --> 53:27.829
Dad gave up being a gold medalist
for his daughter Geum-myeong.

53:28.371 --> 53:30.457
-Maybe she'll be a soccer player.
-[Ae-sun chuckles]

53:30.540 --> 53:31.708
[Gwan-sik] Look at her legs.

53:32.417 --> 53:33.251
You know what?

53:33.335 --> 53:36.630
I hope she becomes
a teacher of literature, Gwan-sik.

53:38.632 --> 53:39.799
I wonder what she'll become.

53:40.467 --> 53:41.426
[Ae-sun] I wonder.

53:44.262 --> 53:48.725
[Geum-myeong] Springtime for them
wasn't a season to realize their dreams,

53:48.808 --> 53:50.602
but to give them up for good.

53:56.858 --> 53:59.236
And they did it willingly.

54:01.404 --> 54:06.201
GEUM-MYEONG, OUR ETERNAL NOSTALGIA

54:07.535 --> 54:10.121
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

54:10.205 --> 54:13.250
Hello. Mind answering a few questions?

54:13.333 --> 54:14.292
-Oh.
-Yes.

54:14.376 --> 54:17.629
So you're here to see the flowers today.
What's going through your mind?

54:17.712 --> 54:20.966
[man] Well, the flowers remind me
of my first love.

54:21.049 --> 54:23.009
[reporter] Ah, first love. Of course.

54:23.093 --> 54:24.511
[woman] Go live with her, then.

54:25.512 --> 54:27.681
-[reporter] Oh, okay.
-Hye-ran. That's dirty. It's dirty.

54:27.764 --> 54:29.349
Thank you for the interview.

54:29.432 --> 54:32.269
-Okay, so let's have another interview.
-Hye-ran, it's dirty. It's dirty.

54:32.352 --> 54:33.561
Come here. Let's go.

54:33.645 --> 54:36.606
[reporter] Oh, hello.
You must be newlyweds.

54:36.690 --> 54:38.942
-[man 2] Yes, that's right.
-[reporter] Congratulations.

54:39.025 --> 54:41.027
[wistful music playing]

54:42.028 --> 54:45.949
These ones… aren't my grandmother's.
They're mine, you know?

54:46.032 --> 54:48.410
Your birthday rings aren't yours.
They're your mother's.

54:48.493 --> 54:51.246
But I really wanted a ring
to propose to her, and…

54:51.329 --> 54:53.331
[groans] You're both so stubborn.

54:56.126 --> 54:57.627
Don't look at me like that.

54:58.795 --> 55:00.714
I actually snuck out for this, so, uh…

55:02.257 --> 55:03.550
If you could finish by tomorrow…

55:03.633 --> 55:06.553
You expect me to work all night
just because you said please, kid?

55:14.144 --> 55:15.729
All right, leave them.

55:18.064 --> 55:20.775
No girl will live with a man
who won't give her a ring.

55:29.993 --> 55:32.120
Is the toilet clean?

55:32.203 --> 55:34.205
Huh? Yeah.

55:35.540 --> 55:36.624
It's completely fine.

55:42.505 --> 55:44.966
A new ring, a new dress.

55:45.050 --> 55:47.385
This will be
a real celebrity wedding, huh?

55:51.389 --> 55:52.390
Is this the one you want?

55:52.474 --> 55:55.602
[Gye-ok] You're not walking down
the runway at a fashion show.

55:55.685 --> 55:58.188
Just rent out an outfit. My goodness.

55:58.772 --> 56:01.775
Whatever you want.
It's up to you what to wear.

56:01.858 --> 56:04.903
[groans] With a hat that big,
you might as well join the circus.

56:04.986 --> 56:06.404
If you want it, take it.

56:06.905 --> 56:08.281
[Gye-ok] Goodness gracious.

56:09.657 --> 56:10.742
[Gwan-sik] You like it?

56:12.160 --> 56:12.994
[Ae-sun] Mm.

56:13.495 --> 56:16.998
I'll expect you wanna move out?
If you have the money, go ahead.

56:17.874 --> 56:19.167
What should I do with my hair?

56:20.877 --> 56:23.755
Should I put it up under the hat
or wear it down?

56:24.714 --> 56:25.757
Huh?

56:25.840 --> 56:26.966
[Ae-sun] My hair.

56:27.050 --> 56:29.052
Should I put my hair up or wear it down?

56:32.389 --> 56:34.474
-Well, don't you think…
-Uh-huh?

56:34.974 --> 56:37.185
Mm, are you sure,

56:38.269 --> 56:39.312
years from now,

56:39.938 --> 56:41.773
you won't regret the hat?

56:42.273 --> 56:43.108
Why?

56:45.068 --> 56:46.444
I just think it could,

56:48.279 --> 56:49.114
uh,

56:50.156 --> 56:52.784
embarrass you maybe?

56:55.245 --> 56:56.454
[scoffs]

56:56.538 --> 56:58.123
So you're a fashion expert now?

56:58.206 --> 56:59.999
Have you even heard of André Kim?

57:00.542 --> 57:01.376
No, not really.

57:04.254 --> 57:06.881
If you're moving out,
do it as soon as possible.

57:06.965 --> 57:08.216
Oh my gosh.

57:09.717 --> 57:11.094
-Hmm? Mm.
-[Gwan-sik chuckles]

57:12.178 --> 57:15.807
Hey. Can we have
quail noodle soup after this?

57:15.890 --> 57:17.392
You just had it yesterday,

57:17.892 --> 57:19.060
little piggy.

57:19.144 --> 57:20.645
[Ae-sun groans, chuckles]

57:22.981 --> 57:24.190
[Gye-ok sighs]

57:26.276 --> 57:27.235
It's cute.

57:27.318 --> 57:28.361
[Ae-sun chuckles]

57:29.404 --> 57:31.239
[camera shutter clicks]

57:31.322 --> 57:34.576
[Geum-myeong] Mom,
what were you thinking with that hat?

57:34.659 --> 57:36.744
Were they punishing you or something?

57:39.456 --> 57:41.458
[feel-good jazz music playing]

01:00:25.246 --> 01:00:29.250
"THE SAME SKY, THE SAME STARS,
ETCHED IN THE SAME HEARTS."

01:00:37.050 --> 01:00:38.885
[music ends]
